    <selectionEntry name="Detachment" id="5218-339c-eb34-9ac0" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="fa39-186d-7b19-c693" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="min" value="1"/>
        <constraint id="1529-f82f-13b6-2da3" field="selections" includeChildForces="true" includeChildSelections="true" scope="roster" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
      </constraints>
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink name="Configuration" id="1cd7-3d59-2550-21a2" hidden="false" primary="true" targetId="4ac9-fd30-1e3d-b249"/>
      </categoryLinks>
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="Detachment" id="3c1b-168f-46ec-21a4" hidden="false">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="feec-1099-4986-a0d3" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" type="min" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <selectionEntries>
            <selectionEntry name="Lions of the Emperor" id="3b75-a700-050c-06f5" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="eca9-0053-41ea-a9c5" field="selections" includeChildSelections="true" scope="force" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="On Gilded Wings" id="199e-d30a-9d03-5da1" hidden="false">
                  <description>At the end of your opponent's Fight phase, you may use this ability:
  For each friendly ADEPTUS CUSTODES TERMINATOR unit: While the unit is unengaged, the unit can be placed into Strategic Reserves.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink name="Disruption" id="4f79-7b5a-83af-75fb" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="ecf8-cf72-7d5b-1b5b"/>
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="51b2-306e-1021-d207" value="0"/>
                <cost name="Detachment Points" typeId="82ae-1066-5107-6ae0" value="1"/>
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Auric Champions" id="a36b-bb22-1a15-2a48" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="f8b0-0d46-c921-9cbb" field="selections" includeChildSelections="true" scope="force" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Assemblage of Might" id="3d49-6705-9d4f-8af1" hidden="false">
                  <description>You can: During the Command phase, in your turn, until the start of your next Command phase:
  -&gt; Select one enemy unit:
    -&gt; That unit is marked as assemblage of might.
    -&gt; While the target is tagged assemblage of might, all friendly ADEPTUS CUSTODES CHARACTER models get +1 to Wound rolls.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink name="Purge the Foe" id="f959-5886-12d0-4f0e" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="6fe0-3dbe-f7e0-10bb"/>
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="51b2-306e-1021-d207" value="0"/>
                <cost name="Detachment Points" typeId="82ae-1066-5107-6ae0" value="1"/>
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Null Maiden Vigil" id="d3ee-47e1-4540-dfe5" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="92c4-5b79-2162-bb03" field="selections" includeChildSelections="true" scope="force" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Silent Sisterhood" id="3876-9ed2-a988-7783" hidden="false">
                  <description>All friendly ANATHEMA PSYKANA CHARACTER models can be your Warlord.
All friendly PROSECUTOR SQUAD units gain the BATTLELINE keyword.
All friendly ANATHEMA PSYKANA units gain the Creeping Dread (Aura) ability:
  -&gt; At the start of the Battle Shock step in your opponent's turn: while an enemy unit is within 12" of this unit, if the unit has the PSYKER keyword or while the unit is below its starting strength, that unit must take a Battle-shock test, applying -1 to that test.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink name="Disruption" id="bea1-1319-3ab4-1e39" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="ecf8-cf72-7d5b-1b5b"/>
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="51b2-306e-1021-d207" value="0"/>
                <cost name="Detachment Points" typeId="82ae-1066-5107-6ae0" value="1"/>
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Might of the Moritoi" id="1bb5-5aba-6c8f-7afc" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="3420-5904-0d91-04f4" field="selections" includeChildSelections="true" scope="force" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Moritoi Ancients" id="95b8-d58d-e2c5-8d19" hidden="false">
                  <description>Unless a friendly ADEPTUS CUSTODES DREADNOUGHT unit is below its starting strength, add 2 to that unit's Objective Control characteristic.
While a friendly ADEPTUS CUSTODES DREADNOUGHT unit is below its starting strength, you can re-roll a Hit roll of 1 for attacks made by that unit.
While a friendly ADEPTUS CUSTODES DREADNOUGHT unit is below half strength:
  -&gt; You can re-roll a Hit roll of 1 for attacks made by that unit.
  -&gt; You can re-roll a Wound roll of 1 for attacks made by that unit.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink name="Take and Hold" id="58f7-e295-7a29-061e" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="1cc1-f11a-4e8f-1bcc"/>
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="51b2-306e-1021-d207" value="0"/>
                <cost name="Detachment Points" typeId="82ae-1066-5107-6ae0" value="1"/>
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Aquilan Shield" id="f82a-5355-0598-8fb8" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="7537-9ecd-bcc8-1058" field="selections" includeChildSelections="true" scope="force" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Gilded Guardians" id="85ba-d51a-10bb-445c" hidden="false">
                  <description>While the target is within range of an objective marker, against ranged attacks, while the target is a friendly ADEPTUS CUSTODES unit (excluding MONSTER or VEHICLE units), when the attack's S is more than the target's T, the attacking unit gets -1 to Wound rolls.
While the Salvus option of Martial Katah is active, add 6 to the Range characteristic of ranged weapons equipped by models in this unit.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink name="Take and Hold" id="616f-c3d5-67d7-2f78" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="1cc1-f11a-4e8f-1bcc"/>
                <categoryLink name="Detachment Tag: shield-host" id="9caf-7c4d-597e-5a70" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="869d-3286-821c-7eac"/>
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="51b2-306e-1021-d207" value="0"/>
                <cost name="Detachment Points" typeId="82ae-1066-5107-6ae0" value="1"/>
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Dread Host" id="385f-36b3-f98d-9735" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="f2da-7411-5710-4a56" field="selections" includeChildSelections="true" scope="force" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Instruments of the Emperor's Wrath" id="9266-4c47-ac20-362c" hidden="false">
                  <description>You can re-roll the Charge roll for all friendly ADEPTUS CUSTODES units.
While the Dacatarai option of Martial Katah is active, while an enemy unit is within Engagement Range of the unit, subtract 2" from that unit's Pile-in and Consolidation moves.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink name="Purge the Foe" id="2a70-0fc9-1629-0580" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="6fe0-3dbe-f7e0-10bb"/>
                <categoryLink name="Detachment Tag: shield-host" id="7267-29b1-34b4-43c9" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="869d-3286-821c-7eac"/>
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="51b2-306e-1021-d207" value="0"/>
                <cost name="Detachment Points" typeId="82ae-1066-5107-6ae0" value="1"/>
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Emissaries Imperatus" id="8d91-29a0-9690-b603" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="0fb7-2fac-05cd-ca76" field="selections" includeChildSelections="true" scope="force" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Heralds of the Throne" id="51f3-bc21-24ad-f927" hidden="false">
                  <description>All friendly ADEPTUS CUSTODES units gain the Fights First ability.
While the Conversai option of Martial Katah is active:
  -&gt; Until the end of the turn: the unit is eligible to start an Action even if it Advanced this turn or it Fell Back this turn.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink name="Priority Assets" id="c2a7-5224-9a30-9e5d" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="0936-9767-1cc7-52ae"/>
                <categoryLink name="Detachment Tag: shield-host" id="3c06-90e4-1b4a-2522" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="869d-3286-821c-7eac"/>
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
                <cost name="pts" typeId="51b2-306e-1021-d207" value="0"/>
                <cost name="Detachment Points" typeId="82ae-1066-5107-6ae0" value="1"/>
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry name="Emperor's Chosen" id="1c7e-56bc-3196-b5cd" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
              <constraints>
                <constraint id="3797-b09c-912c-4dd1" field="selections" includeChildSelections="true" scope="force" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule name="Magna Imperator" id="de91-8635-62aa-9929" hidden="false">
                  <description>-&gt; When a friendly unit is selected to shoot or fight (the triggering unit must have ADEPTUS CUSTODES):
  -&gt; You can re-roll one Hit roll.
  -&gt; You can re-roll one Wound roll.
-&gt; You can: while the Rendax option of Martial Katah is active, select one enemy unit with the MONSTER or VEHICLE keyword if the selected unit is within Engagement Range of the unit: roll one D6: on 1-2, that unit suffers 1 mortal wound; on 3-5, that unit suffers D3 mortal wounds; on 6, that unit suffers 3 mortal wounds.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <categoryLinks>
                <categoryLink name="Priority Assets" id="8dc3-cbd7-bdda-c031" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="0936-9767-1cc7-52ae"/>
                <categoryLink name="Detachment Tag: shield-host" id="844c-f2f3-05b0-1db9" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="869d-3286-821c-7eac"/>
              </categoryLinks>
              <costs>
