  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Aegis of the Emperor" id="7374-6ade-4df1-fc0a" hidden="false">
      <description>All friendly ADEPTUS CUSTODES units with the Aegis of the Emperor ability have the Feel No Pain 5+ ability against mortal wounds.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Aquila Commander" id="34bc-08ad-00f6-7a0a" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of the battle round, while this model has the Aquila Commander ability, while this model is the Warlord, you gain 1CP.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Daughters of the Abyss" id="1855-3f49-c996-2b92" hidden="false">
      <description>All friendly ANATHEMA PSYKANA units have the Feel No Pain 3+ ability against Psychic Attacks.
All friendly ANATHEMA PSYKANA units gain the Psychic Null ability:
  -&gt; While a friendly ADEPTUS CUSTODES unit is within 6" of this unit, that unit has the Feel No Pain 5+ ability against Psychic Attacks.
Your army can include ANATHEMA PSYKANA units.
You cannot select Anathema Psykana as your Army Faction.
All friendly ANATHEMA PSYKANA units cannot be your Warlord.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Martial Ka'tah" id="9356-9dd6-9900-f9c7" hidden="false">
      <description>-&gt; At the start of your Command phase: all friendly ADEPTUS CUSTODES units with the Martial Katah ability are readied.
-&gt; You can: while the unit is readied, select one: Conversai (until the end of the turn: the unit is no longer readied; during the Command phase, in your turn, the unit is eligible to start an Action even if it is within Engagement Range of enemy units or it is Battle-shocked; the unit is eligible to shoot even if it is performing an Action) / Calistus (when the unit is selected to move, until the end of the phase: the unit is no longer readied; during the Movement phase, in your turn, the unit can move over models as though they were not there, during its Normal, Advance and Fall Back moves) / Salvus (when the unit is selected to shoot, until the end of the phase: the unit is no longer readied; during the Shooting phase, in your turn, the unit ignores any modifiers to its Ballistic Skill characteristics; the unit ignores any modifiers to its Hit and Wound rolls) / Dacatarai (at the start of the Fight phase, until the end of the phase: the unit is no longer readied; while making melee attacks, while the target is an enemy unit (excluding MONSTER or VEHICLE units), you can re-roll a Hit roll of 1 with melee weapons) / Kaptaris (at the start of the Fight phase, until the end of the phase: the unit is no longer readied; against melee attacks, the attacking unit gets -1 to Hit rolls) / Rendax (when the unit is selected to fight, until the end of the phase: the unit is no longer readied; during the Fight phase, against MONSTER or VEHICLE targets, melee weapons equipped by models in this unit gain [LETHAL HITS]).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Special Move Types" id="75a8-6c0d-0448-faaa" hidden="false">
      <description>Shock Disembark Move (the Shock mode of a Disembark move):
  - Each model is set up wholly within 3" of that Transport.
  - A unit can make this move only if the unit is embarked and the Transport this unit is embarked within is on the battlefield and the unit did not embark this phase.
  - After it moves, until the end of the turn: the unit cannot declare a charge.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
